Z||000000||Spektyr||04-24-2001||02:08 PM||||My poor buddy... all excited about me getting my Fiero so he'd have someone to race in his '90 Laser RS.<P>He led onto the highway (he got in his car first, I just tucked in behind.)  I slipped easily to the fast lane and just opened her up.  Thanks to my 85mph speedo I can't quote any speeds, but it was 90+.<P>My 85GT easily outran him before I dropped back to 70mph.<P>Now he don't wanna play no more.  But then he thinks he's driving an American car, too.  Silly Mitsu motor.  Shoulda let him win so I could REALLY school him when I get done with the car.<P>Or maybe it was that I waved 'bye-bye' through the sunroof as he sucked my exhaust...<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||6
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||04-24-2001||03:18 PM||||Hey at least you didn't stick you hand out the window and motion him forward to catch up with you, only to pull out further while hes flooring it.<P>I love doing that to Hondas...||||reg||6
Z||000002||fyerstarter||04-24-2001||05:26 PM||||Hrm... was this the turbo version? Because I am the former owner of a 90 Laser RS Turbo and it would smoke the doors off any stock v6 fiero any day of the week. <P>v6 Fiero<BR>140 hp<BR>16.2 qtr mile<P>90 Laser/Eclipse/Talon turbo<BR>190 hp<BR>15.4 qtr mile<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Spektyr||04-25-2001||03:58 PM||||Actually, the 90 turbos were rated at 195hp.  And yes, this is the turbo version, but the child driving it has blown his exhaust-side turbo gaskets.  He had his turbo until he hit the end of the ramp, and then his manifold heated up enough to break what little seal he has left.<P>(ie. he has the turbo till the motor warms up and the metal stretches).<P>Actually, every '90 Laser RS had the turbo, it was standard on them.  Yes, he will smoke me when he gets his turbo fixed, but that's assuming he doesn't smoke his clutch, blow the CV's, throw a rod, or something equally stupid before then.  He drives the hell out of the car when he should be babying it until he gets it fixed.<P>Not to mention he's going to fix the front clip before the turbo (strange priorities).<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
